<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zorawar Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1841</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zorawar Singh Kahluria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zorawar Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> general in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a>. Between 1834 and 1840 he conquered Ladakh and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltistan">Baltistan</a>, bringing them into the Dogra realm that later became the princely state of Jammu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>. He then invaded western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and was killed in battle against Tibetan and Qing forces in 1841.</p></div>
